   "created_at": "2018-02-24T22:31:47Z",
   "updated_at": "2018-02-24T22:31:47Z",
   "body": "@fpietrosanti - One alternative that you might consider (and @konklone, maybe we should consider getting this into domain-scan somehow?) is https://testssl.sh / https://github.com/drwetter/testssl.sh/ which does a lot more of the types of checks that @konklone alluded to.\r\n\r\nIt doesn't spit out a specific grade rating, but it does hit most if not all of the same types of things that SSL Labs provides.\r\n\r\nFor instance, we use it internally for doing an SSL Labs-like scan against our internal resources that SSL Labs wouldn't be able to reach. Perhaps that is a similar reason as to why you're looking for this to be incorporated into pshtt?",
   "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
